sequenceDiagram
  %% process.restart on the Gateway engine: the `process` family, with a restart that runs at most once per Operation even when a receipt is lost and the executor's journal no longer holds the result. Design for ADR 0267 and ADR 0271; no engine flow exists yet. Step names describe effects; the implementation settles action names unless an existing action is named.
  %% A restart is not a desired state, so the step carries evidence of the run it replaces: systemd's InvocationID with the boot ID, or Docker's container StartedAt. A changed value proves a restart already happened, and the step reports it instead of restarting again.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:restart
  %% kind: process.restart
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Target Node<br/>executor
  CLI->>GW: process:restart 417
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: provisioning
  %%> Same admission as process/restart.mmd; Vite plans, Gateway release-container and Instance-container Processes throw `EngineUnsupported` until the `process` family covers them, as process/engine/start.mmd
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `process.restart` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: the `process` family's read and restart actions
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    EN->>N: Read the running instance<br/>unit · boot ID · InvocationID
    %%> Step `read`: read-only; systemd `InvocationID`, `ActiveState` and `/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id` (Docker: `State.StartedAt` and the container ID)
    %%> Its receipt output is pinned into the restart step's input when that step is first built; a resend reuses the pinned value
    N-->>EN: Evidence<br/>output: boot ID · invocation
    EN->>N: Restart if unchanged<br/>compare, then restart
    %%> Step `restart`, under the Process's target lock: reads the evidence again; only when it equals the pinned evidence does it apply the boot policy and run `systemctl restart` (Docker: `docker container restart`)
    %%> Evidence changed (this Operation already restarted it, or the unit restarted by itself since the read): no restart; the receipt says `restarted: already` with the new evidence
    %%> A different boot ID means the Node rebooted after the read: the unit already runs a fresh instance, so the step only converges it to running
    N-->>EN: New evidence<br/>active · new InvocationID
    %%> Verification read-back: active, the boot policy as admitted, and an InvocationID (or StartedAt) different from the pinned one; otherwise `process.restart_unverified`
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> Within the journal's replay window: `done` for this step answers the stored result with `repeat: true`; nothing runs again
      %%> After compaction or a lost journal: the step runs, finds the evidence changed and reports `already`; a second restart never happens
      %%> The Operation keeps its lock throughout, so Process 417 stays fenced from other Operations
      N-->>EN: Restarted already<br/>no second restart
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record Process active<br/>status · restarted
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>desired state unchanged
      %%> - a failed `read` changed nothing; a failed `restart` left the unit as systemd reports it, and the retry is a new Operation with a fresh read
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-process-control
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-process-control (process/restart.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
